# ace2 S-only Rerun Agent Guide

## Scope

This file governs the execution repository at
`zhong@ace2:~/Documents/pms-mamba-financial-forecasting` for the S-only manuscript
review handoff dated 2026-08-11. Read the full review and protocol before changing
code, configuration, results, or manuscript-facing documentation:

`docs/manuscript_review_s_only_rerun_guidance_20260811.md`

The current paper scope is target-only (`_s`) univariate financial level forecasting
with the model named **Regime-Gated Mamba**. The historical S/MS material is preserved
in the Gitee checkpoint `30b6a4758b0db655812e8e0f81efbc99b63c0366`; do not copy it
back into the active paper evidence release.

## Current Status

- The last recorded remote state was `main` at
  `f5a694d3f18565af2cd46a6f7005027d92c13a1f`, clean, on 2026-08-11 16:33 +08:00.
  This is historical only: run a fresh preflight before any work.
- The local review release is
  `reproducibility/financial_s_only_review_v0`; it is an interim post hoc audit, not
  submission evidence.
- Do not treat 2023--2026 as untouched or prospective testing.
- Do not rely on `docs/model_reference.md` for implementation facts until it is
  reconciled with the active code and configuration.

## Required Behavior

1. Before any operation, record `pwd`, branch, full commit, `git status --short`,
   relevant processes, GPU status, free disk space, and result/log modification times.
2. Do not start, stop, restart, or alter a run unless the human author explicitly
   authorizes that operation. This handoff provides guidance only; it is not run
   authorization.
3. When a run is authorized, use only the four target-only tasks:
   `financial_cross_asset_s`, `financial_crypto_s`, `financial_fx_s`, and
   `financial_yields_s`; use horizons 1, 5, 20, 60, 120, 252 and seeds 2023--2027.
4. Run the three deterministic references (Last-value, random-walk-with-drift, ARIMA)
   with the same target dates, inverse transformation, and RMSSE denominator as the
   learned models. Do not combine old reference rows with a new learned-model campaign.
5. Treat the implemented `regime_linear` branch as the current model. With one input
   channel, two gate summary features are identically zero. First audit it unchanged.
   Any non-degenerate time-statistics redesign is a new model requiring a new identity,
   a 2022-or-earlier selection record, and retrospective labeling.
6. Keep model inclusion, primary metric, uncertainty method, and task/horizon weighting
   fixed before results are inspected. Record all exclusions and failures.
7. Publish a new compact release only after the matrix is complete and stable, under
   `reproducibility/financial_s_only_retrospective_v1/`, including protocol, data
   hashes, model map, per-seed learned metrics, deterministic metrics, aggregate and
   paired-comparison tables, release status, claim-evidence map, and `SHA256SUMS`.
8. Do not overwrite historical releases, modify the protected evaluation boundary, rerun
   HPO, delete results, or claim superiority/efficiency without explicit authorization
   and frozen evidence.

After a completed release, provide the path, branch, commit, dirty state, file count,
byte total, SHA-256 verification result, and any protocol deviations to the local paper
repository before manuscript numbers are changed.
